_impact"": ""We donate 1% of our time, product, and profit to those who need it most: our 1-1-1 model."", ""employee_wellbeing_development"": ""We take care of ourselves and each other first, so we can do more for our customers.""}",0,2,1,2,1,1,1,1,0,2,1,0
CRM,Salesforce,Technology,2018,"The Fourth Industrial Revolution is changing the way people work, using robotics, AI, the Internet of Things, and more. By making these innovations easier and more accessible, we're helping create a future with greater opportunity and equality for all.
Trailblazers don't fear change, we embrace it. We harness new technologies to entirely transform our companies, our careers, and hopefully, our world.
In Hawaiian culture, “Ohana” means family; it's the tie that binds people together. Our Ohana is built on four core values that inspire us to work together every day toward improving the world.
In 1999, we pioneered CRM software in the cloud, helping 150,000+ companies run their business smarter. Today, we're creating a whole new economy that's helping millions of Salesforce users improve their lives, too.
Everyday, more than 150,000 companies just like yours are increasing employee productivity, team collaboration, customer loyalty and, most importantly, their sales using the world’s #1 CRM platform.
Our innovative cloud-based platform gets accolades from press around the world, but it’s the dedication to helping our customers succeed that's made us the world’s 4th-largest software company.
*From FORTUNE® Magazine, March 15, 2017 © 2017 Time Inc. FORTUNE and 100 Best Companies to Work For are registered trademarks and are used under License. FORTUNE and Time Inc. are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of, Salesforce.",True,collaboration_teamwork;community_social_impact;customer_focus;innovation;performance_results,"Introduces 'Fourth Industrial Revolution', 'robotics, AI', and 'greater opportunity and equality for all', and the core values are cut to 'four core values'. Emphasis shifts from the 1-1-1 model and award lists to customer productivity and '150,000+ companies', with the phrase 'Trailblazers don't fear change' appearing.",ok,,salesforce.com/company,1,20180104004637,https://web.archive.org/web/20180104004637id_/https://www.salesforce.com/company/,225,2017,0.0703,substantive,"The 2018 page drops the 2017 self-description around the 1-1-1 philanthropy model, employee respect and culture statements and eight core values, replacing them with framing around the Fourth Industrial Revolution, Trailblazers, Ohana with four values, and customer success.",False,Reads as a marketing/landing page with promotional copy and an analyst-ranking disclaimer rather than a general company overview; it is a campaign-style page about the company's vision and products.,"{""innovation"": ""We harness new technologies to entirely transform our companies, our careers, and hopefully, our world."", ""customer_focus"": ""it's the dedication to helping our customers succeed that's made us the world's 4th-largest software company."", ""collaboration_teamwork"": ""Our Ohana is built on four core values that inspire us to work together every day toward improving the world."", ""performance_results"": ""Everyday, more than 150,000 companies just like yours are increasing employee productivity, team collaboration, customer loyalty and, most importantly, their sales"", ""community_social_impact"": ""By making these innovations easier and more accessible, we're helping create a future with greater opportunity and equality for all.""}",0,2,0,2,1,1,0,0,0,1,0,0
