F,Ford Motor,Consumer Discretionary,2016,"Our Company
At Ford, we go further to make our cars better, our employees happier and our planet a better place to be. Learn more about the work that makes Ford a company that we’re proud to be a part of.

SCROLL TO EXPLORE

Ford is dedicated to building great products to strengthen our business and benefit our communities.
- Quality Improving quality is a daily priority at Ford. From design and manufacture to sales and service, Ford always aims to increase customer satisfaction.
- Safe We have a longstanding commitment to developing and implementing innovations that make our vehicles safer for our customers and their families.
- Green Ford’s sustainability strategy goes beyond reducing CO₂ emissions. From water usage to worker rights, we’ve made sustainability an integral part of our business.
- Smart Innovation is at the core of our company. Ford is pioneering the extensive use of high-strength aluminum in a mass-market vehicle, and in 2014 we will host the auto industry’s first developer conference for in-car connectivity.
Ford is committed to developing great products for customers around the world. In 2014, we are introducing 23 new vehicles globally. Ford saw the largest percentage point gain in U.S. market share among automakers in 2013. In addition, Ford F-Series was the best-selling vehicle in the United States for the 32nd year in a row and Ford Focus was the best-selling nameplate in the world. With the freshest car portfolio in the industry and a commitment to deliver continuous improvement for fuel economy, Ford is well positioned in the global marketplace
Shop Online
Great vehicles are great for drivers everywhere, and that’s the foundation of our business’s strength. To meet demand, Ford is in the midst of its most ambitious manufacturing expansion in 50 years. We’re increasing capacity in the United States and adding plants around the world.
We’re growing without sacrificing profits. In the past year, we’ve continued to fund our employee pension plans worldwide, delivered record profit-sharing contributions to our U.S. hourly employees and doubled our shareholder dividend.
Learn more about our business:
2014 Annual Report
Investors
Our work doesn’t stop with our products and our bottom line. An integral part of the Ford team’s DNA is ‘people serving people.’ That’s why our global brand promise is called Go Further – we go further so you can.
We’re helping to solve global challenges linked to economic development, energy security and environmental sustainability. In 2013, for example, Ford globally reduced the amount of water it used to produce each vehicle by 30 percent compared to a 2009 baseline, reaching its goal two years ahead of schedule. Plans are under way to set new long-term goals.
Community service is an important part of Ford’s heritage and always has been. The Ford Volunteer Corps celebrated its 10th anniversary in 2015. Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services has donated more than $1.5 billion in its 65-year history.
Within our Sustainability report, our Blueprint for Mobility envisions the future of transportation, in which vehicles communicate with each other and the world around them to make driving safer, easier and more efficient. Our Blueprint for Sustainability goes beyond improved fuel economy and reduced CO2 emissions to define sustainability as a business model that creates value by preserving and enhancing environmental, social and financial capital.
Learn more about our efforts:
Community
Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services
Sustainability Report
2014 was a successful step forward in furthering our One Ford plan to deliver profitable growth for all. Despite a challenging environment, particularly in South America and Russia, and an unprecedented number of product launches, the company’s fifth consecutive year of pre-tax profit and positive automotive operating-related cash flow reflects our continued focus on our One Ford plan.
We are driving to be both a product company and a mobility company. Our vision is nothing less than to change the way the world moves. At Ford, we view this as the ultimate opportunity. In fact it is as big of an opportunity as when our founder put the world on wheels more than a century ago.
As our company grows, the Ford Fund is growing along with it to better serve the communities around the world where we do business. Learn more about hte great work Ford, its employees and dealers are doing to help create a better world.",,collaboration_teamwork;community_social_impact;customer_focus;employee_wellbeing_development;environment_sustainability;innovation;performance_results;respect_people;safety,"Baseline framing is product- and growth-led: 'dedicated to building great products', four pillars (Quality, Safe, Green, Smart), new-vehicle counts, market share, and profit assurances ('We're growing without sacrificing profits'), alongside 'One Ford plan to deliver profitable growth for all' and 'a product company and a mobility company'.",ok,,corporate.ford.com/company.html,1,20160113141630,https://web.archive.org/web/20160113141630id_/http://corporate.ford.com:80/company.html?,725,,,no_prior,,True,"Company overview page ('Our Company') describing products, values, sustainability, community and business strategy.","{""customer_focus"": ""Quality Improving quality is a daily priority at Ford. From design and manufacture to sales and service, Ford always aims to increase customer satisfaction."", ""innovation"": ""Smart Innovation is at the core of our company. Ford is pioneering the extensive use of high-strength aluminum in a mass-market vehicle"", ""environment_sustainability"": ""Green Ford’s sustainability strategy goes beyond reducing CO₂ emissions. From water usage to worker rights, we’ve made sustainability an integral part of our business."", ""safety"": ""Safe We have a longstanding commitment to developing and implementing innovations that make our vehicles safer for our customers and their families."", ""performance_results"": ""We’re growing without sacrificing profits. In the past year, we’ve continued to fund our employee pension plans worldwide, delivered record profit-sharing contributions"", ""community_social_impact"": ""Community service is an important part of Ford’s heritage and always has been. The Ford Volunteer Corps celebrated its 10th anniversary in 2015."", ""respect_people"": ""An integral part of the Ford team’s DNA is ‘people serving people.’"", ""employee_wellbeing_development"": ""we make our cars better, our employees happier and our planet a better place to be."", ""collaboration_teamwork"": ""we’re growing without sacrificing profits.""}",1,2,0,2,1,2,1,0,2,2,1,2
F,Ford Motor,Consumer Discretionary,2017,"Our Company
At Ford, we go further to make our cars better, our employees happier and our planet a better place to be. Learn more about the work that makes Ford a company that we’re proud to be a part of.

SCROLL TO EXPLORE

People working together as a lean, global enterprise to make people’s lives better through automotive and mobility leadership.
- Quality Improving quality is a daily priority at Ford. From design and manufacture to sales and service, Ford always aims to increase customer satisfaction.
- Safe We have a longstanding commitment to developing and implementing innovations that make our vehicles safer for our customers and their families.
- Green Ford’s sustainability strategy goes beyond reducing CO₂ emissions. From water usage to worker rights, we’ve made sustainability an integral part of our business.
- Smart Innovation is at the core of our company. Ford is pioneering the extensive use of high-strength aluminum in a mass-market vehicle, and in 2014 we will host the auto industry’s first developer conference for in-car connectivity.
Great vehicles are great for drivers everywhere, and that’s the foundation of our business’s strength. To meet demand, Ford is in the midst of its most ambitious manufacturing expansion in 50 years. We’re increasing capacity in the United States and adding plants around the world.
We’re growing without sacrificing profits. In the past year, we’ve continued to fund our employee pension plans worldwide, delivered record profit-sharing contributions to our U.S. hourly employees and doubled our shareholder dividend.
Learn more about our business:
2015 Annual Report
Investors
Our work doesn’t stop with our products and our bottom line. An integral part of the Ford team’s DNA is ‘people serving people.’ That’s why our global brand promise is called Go Further – we go further so you can.
We’re helping to solve global challenges linked to economic development, energy security and environmental sustainability. In 2013, for example, Ford globally reduced the amount of water it used to produce each vehicle by 30 percent compared to a 2009 baseline, reaching its goal two years ahead of schedule. Plans are under way to set new long-term goals.
Community service is an important part of Ford’s heritage and always has been. The Ford Volunteer Corps celebrated its 10th anniversary in 2015. Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services has donated more than $1.5 billion in its 65-year history.
Within our Sustainability report, our Blueprint for Mobility envisions the future of transportation, in which vehicles communicate with each other and the world around them to make driving safer, easier and more efficient. Our Blueprint for Sustainability goes beyond improved fuel economy and reduced CO2 emissions to define sustainability as a business model that creates value by preserving and enhancing environmental, social and financial capital.
Learn more about our efforts:
Community
Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services
Sustainability Report
We promised that 2015 would be a breakthrough year for the Ford Motor Company, and it was. We delivered record profits. Perhaps even more importantly, we fundamentally began to expand our business model to position Ford to deliver long-term growth and value creation in a rapidly changing world.
Contributing to a better world always has been a core value at Ford, and our commitment to sustainability is a key part of our company DNA. Ultimately, our vision is to make people’s lives better by changing the way the world moves, just as Henry Ford did more than a century ago.
As our company grows, the Ford Fund is growing along with it to better serve the communities around the world where we do business. Learn more about the great work Ford, its employees and dealers are doing to help create a better world.",True,community_social_impact;customer_focus;employee_wellbeing_development;environment_sustainability;innovation;performance_results;respect_people;safety,"Adds the framing 'People working together as a lean, global enterprise to make people's lives better through automotive and mobility leadership' and 'Contributing to a better world always has been a core value'; the 'Ford is dedicated to building great products' line and the four-pillar list are dropped. Profit language shifts to 'record profits' and 'long-term growth and value creation'.",ok,,corporate.ford.com/company.html,1,20170129160702,https://web.archive.org/web/20170129160702id_/http://corporate.ford.com/company.html,619,2016,0.7827,substantive,"The 2017 page adds a mission statement framing Ford as making people's lives better through mobility leadership, adds a new paragraph calling contributing to a better world a core value and describing 2015 as a breakthrough year, and drops the 2016 'Our Company' line emphasizing quality and dealers while updating the report year from 2014 to 2015.",True,"Company overview page with self-description, mission-style statement and values-related content under 'Our Company'.","{""innovation"": ""Smart Innovation is at the core of our company. Ford is pioneering the extensive use of high-strength aluminum in a mass-market vehicle"", ""customer_focus"": ""Ford always aims to increase customer satisfaction."", ""safety"": ""developing and implementing innovations that make our vehicles safer for our customers and their families."", ""environment_sustainability"": ""Our commitment to sustainability is a key part of our company DNA."", ""performance_results"": ""We delivered record profits. Perhaps even more importantly, we fundamentally began to expand our business model to position Ford to deliver long-term growth and value creation"", ""community_social_impact"": ""Contributing to a better world always has been a core value at Ford"", ""respect_people"": ""people serving people."", ""employee_wellbeing_development"": ""delivered record profit-sharing contributions to our U.S. hourly employees and doubled our shareholder dividend.""}",0,2,0,1,0,2,1,0,2,2,1,1
F,Ford Motor,Consumer Discretionary,2018,"Our work doesn’t stop with our products and our bottom line. An integral part of the Ford team’s DNA is ‘people serving people.’ That’s why our global brand promise is called Go Further – we go further so you can.
We’re helping to solve global challenges linked to economic development, energy security and environmental sustainability. In 2013, for example, Ford globally reduced the amount of water it used to produce each vehicle by 30 percent compared to a 2009 baseline, reaching its goal two years ahead of schedule. Plans are under way to set new long-term goals.
Community service is an important part of Ford’s heritage and always has been. The Ford Volunteer Corps celebrated its 10th anniversary in 2015. Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services has donated more than $1.5 billion in its 65-year history.
Within our Sustainability report, our Blueprint for Mobility envisions the future of transportation, in which vehicles communicate with each other and the world around them to make driving safer, easier and more efficient. Our Blueprint for Sustainability goes beyond improved fuel economy and reduced CO2 emissions to define sustainability as a business model that creates value by preserving and enhancing environmental, social and financial capital.
Learn more about our efforts:
Community
Ford Motor Company Fund and Community Services
Sustainability Report",True,community_social_impact;environment_sustainability;innovation;respect_people;safety,"Substantial cut: the company-level product, profit and vision paragraphs are removed, leaving only community, sustainability, 'people serving people' and 'Go Further' brand-promise content. Little new vocabulary is introduced.",ok,,corporate.ford.com/company.html,1,20180107021852,https://web.archive.org/web/20180107021852id_/http://corporate.ford.com:80/company.html,217,2017,0.5191,substantive,"The 2018 page drops the prior quality, safety, green and smart pillars, the growth, profit and shareholder-return messaging, and the claim that innovation is at the core, retaining only community service, sustainability, water reduction and a people-serving brand promise.",True,Excerpt from the company's 'Our Company' overview section; it contains self-description and value statements but covers only community and sustainability content rather than the full overview.,"{""respect_people"": ""An integral part of the Ford team’s DNA is ‘people serving people.’"", ""environment_sustainability"": ""Our Blueprint for Sustainability goes beyond improved fuel economy and reduced CO2 emissions to define sustainability as a business model that creates value by preserving and enhancing environmental, social and financial capital."", ""community_social_impact"": ""Community service is an important part of Ford’s heritage and always has been."", ""innovation"": ""Within our Sustainability report, our Blueprint for Mobility envisions the future of transportation"", ""safety"": ""to make driving safer, easier and more efficient""}",0,1,0,0,0,0,1,0,2,2,0,1
F,Ford Motor,Consumer Discretionary,2019,"Ford Motor Company: Company Information | Ford.com
Our belief:
Freedom of movement drives human progress.
Our aspiration:
To become the world’s most trusted company, designing smart vehicles for a smart world.
Winning Portfolio
We are committed to providing the products our customers want in the markets where we know we can win.
Propulsion Choices
We are committed to producing clean-running cars - without sacrificing the power, style, and performance customers expect.
Autonomous Technology
Our strategy is to build a viable AV business by designing products centered around the needs of humans.
Mobility Experiences
Our goal is to create a set of mobility experiences that win trust, protect data, and address problems of congested cities.
Our history
Our focus on the freedom of movement helped create the middle class with the $5 wage, revolutionized manufacturing with the moving assembly line and got the whole world moving with the first vehicles built for everyone.
About Ford's history
Our leadership
“I believe the purpose of a company is to make people’s lives better. That is how we became great in the past and it is how we will become even greater in the future.”
William Clay Ford Jr.
Executive Chairman, Ford Motor Company
“Breakthrough technologies are transforming nearly every aspect of the vehicles we build and how people use them, demanding a rethink of how we design transportation systems.”
Jim Hackett
President and Chief Executive Officer
More Corporate Governance
Our global operations
Today, Ford Motor Company touches the lives of people in every corner of the globe, not just by making and selling the most technologically advanced, reliable and fun-to-drive vehicles in the world, but by leading the way in manufacturing and business innovation.
Discover where we are",True,community_social_impact;customer_focus;environment_sustainability;innovation;integrity_ethics;performance_results,"Major reframing around a 'Our belief' and 'Our aspiration' structure: 'Freedom of movement drives human progress', 'world's most trusted company, designing smart vehicles for a smart world', plus new terms like 'autonomous technology', 'mobility experiences', 'win trust, protect data' and a William Clay Ford Jr. quote stating 'the purpose of a company is to make people's lives better'.",ok,,corporate.ford.com/company.html,1,20190331012553,https://web.archive.org/web/20190331012553id_/https://corporate.ford.com/company.html,285,2018,0.0637,substantive,"The 2019 page drops the 2018 emphasis on people serving people, community service, water and sustainability reporting, and reframes the company around a belief in freedom of movement, a trust-based aspiration, and autonomous and mobility products.",True,"Corporate company information page covering belief, aspiration, strategy overview, history, leadership and global operations.","{""innovation"": ""Breakthrough technologies are transforming nearly every aspect of the vehicles we build and how people use them, demanding a rethink of how we design transportation systems."", ""integrity_ethics"": ""To become the world’s most trusted company, designing smart vehicles for a smart world."", ""customer_focus"": ""We are committed to providing the products our customers want in the markets where we know we can win."", ""environment_sustainability"": ""We are committed to producing clean-running cars - without sacrificing the power, style, and performance customers expect."", ""performance_results"": ""not just by making and selling the most technologically advanced, reliable and fun-to-drive vehicles in the world, but by leading the way in manufacturing and business innovation."", ""community_social_impact"": ""I believe the purpose of a company is to make people’s lives better.""}",0,2