GOOGL,Alphabet,Technology,2016,"Google’s mission is to organize the world’s information and make it universally accessible and useful.

Ten things we know to be true
#1: Focus on the user and all else will follow.
Since the beginning, we’ve focused on providing the best user experience possible. Whether we’re designing a new Internet browser or a new tweak to the look of the homepage, we take great care to ensure that they will ultimately serve you, rather than our own internal goal or bottom line.
News from Google
Read up on our latest news, browse our blog directory, or choose to follow a number of Google+ pages for updates on various products and initiatives.
Google careers
Ever wondered what life at Google looks like or what benefits you might expect as a Googler? Search for a job at Google or check out one of our locations worldwide.
Investor relations
Find out about investor news, financial information or corporate governance.
Doodles
Doodles are the fun, surprising and sometimes spontaneous changes that are made to the Google logo to celebrate holidays, anniversaries and the lives of famous artists, pioneers and scientists.
Google Ventures
Google Ventures is an independent venture capital fund financed by Google. With $300 million to invest each year, the team looks to find and invest in the most disruptive and interesting startup founders.",,customer_focus;employee_wellbeing_development;innovation;performance_results,"Baseline framing is user-centric and product-led: the mission to 'organize the world's information' is paired with 'Focus on the user and all else will follow' and the claim that designs 'ultimately serve you, rather than our own internal goal or bottom line'. Investor relations, careers, Doodles and Google Ventures appear as site sections.",ok,,google.com/intl/en/about.html,1,20160101005438,https://web.archive.org/web/20160101005438id_/http://www.google.com/intl/en/about.html,221,,,no_prior,,True,"Presents Google's mission and a 'Ten things we know to be true' statement of principles, but is largely a navigation hub with news, careers, investor relations and Doodles links; reads as a corporate overview page with mixed navigation content.","{""customer_focus"": ""we take great care to ensure that they will ultimately serve you, rather than our own internal goal or bottom line"", ""innovation"": ""the most disruptive and interesting startup founders"", ""employee_wellbeing_development"": ""Ever wondered what life at Google looks like or what benefits you might expect as a Googler?"", ""performance_results"": ""Find out about investor news, financial information or corporate governance.""}",0,1,0,2,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,0
